    "description": "<p><strong>Current support-package notice:</strong> the earlier SGA 6 English support ZIP was removed from this version after a wrap-aware audit found reconstructable host-local paths in public text/control files. The corrected 381-page reader PDF remains byte-identical and current. A privacy-clean support archive will return only after regenerated manifests and independent audit.</p><p>This record contains modern LaTeX working editions, source workpasses, translations, and audit material for SGA 1, SGA 5, and SGA 6. The files have different authority levels; broad page coverage does not imply uniform source certification.</p>\n<p><strong>Open first:</strong> the 309-page SGA 5 English source-aware working translation remains the default preview. The record also directly exposes the corrected 381-page SGA 6 full-range layered English reader, the 374-page French SGA 6 source-rescribe checkpoint through source index 684, the French SGA 5 workpass, a four-page Spanish SGA 6 Expose X checkpoint, and the new four-page SGA 1 English checkpoint.</p>\n<p><strong>SGA 1 addition:</strong> file <code>00a</code> is a bounded source-audited English working checkpoint for the Expose I heading/opening and section I.1. Its sole authority is the corrected French TeX in arXiv <code>math/0206203v2</code>, exact main-file lines 556-604. Continuation begins at line 605, section I.2, <em>Morphismes quasi-finis</em>. File <code>07</code> groups all 20 public-safe files: editable TeX, five source/control ledgers, compact build records, four target-page renders, continuation cursor, attribution and scope notes, manifests, and exact hashes.</p>\n<p><strong>SGA 1 boundary:</strong> this is one machine-assisted source-audited working unit. It is not complete SGA 1, a critical edition, peer review, mathematical certification, or independent scholarly certification. External English candidates were wording/adverse controls only and are neither source authority nor independently corroborating witnesses.</p>\n<p><strong>SGA 5 boundary:</strong> the public English reader is substantial source-aware working material, but its readiness audit remains open. Known editorial and source-ambiguity items remain documented; the file is not a critical edition or independent certification of every locus. Historical Spanish SGA 5 checkpoints remain withdrawn pending a canonical rebuild and are absent from this version.</p>\n<p><strong>SGA 6 boundary:</strong> the corrected English reader covers the extant scan with explicit authority layers. The prefix is inherited and partially synchronized; idx532-662 was synchronized against the directly checked French layer available at build time; idx663-702 and terminal matter are scan-checked draft material pending later French reconciliation. The French reader is a source-rescribe checkpoint at idx684, not whole-volume certification. The Spanish file is a bounded four-page tranche.</p>\n<p><strong>Use:</strong> open the reader PDFs first. Use the ZIP files for editable TeX, source/reference material, ledgers, build and render evidence, and checksums. Build success establishes artifact integrity, not mathematical correctness. Verify citation-critical formulas, diagrams, tables, and theorem statements against the included source controls.</p>\n<p><strong>Corrections and continuation:</strong> the inspectable GitHub mirror and correction channel are at <a href=\"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts\">https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts</a>. None of these surfaces is called a critical edition, complete translation, proof check, diagram-by-diagram certification, or whole-SGA completion.</p>",
    "additional_descriptions": [
      {
        "description": "Reader-first SGA 1/5/6 working-edition record. The SGA 6 English reader remains public; its path-leaking support ZIP is absent from the current surface pending a privacy-clean replacement. No critical-edition, proof-checking, or whole-SGA completion claim is made.",
