    "description_stripped": "Current support-package notice: the earlier SGA 6 English support ZIP was removed from this version after a wrap-aware audit found reconstructable host-local paths in public text/control files. The corrected 381-page reader PDF remains byte-identical and current. A privacy-clean support archive will return only after regenerated manifests and independent audit.\nThis record contains modern LaTeX working editions, source workpasses, translations, and audit material for SGA 1, SGA 5, and SGA 6. The files have different authority levels; broad page coverage does not imply uniform source certification.\n\nOpen first: the 309-page SGA 5 English source-aware working translation remains the default preview. The record also directly exposes the corrected 381-page SGA 6 full-range layered English reader, the 374-page French SGA 6 source-rescribe checkpoint through source index 684, the French SGA 5 workpass, a four-page Spanish SGA 6 Expose X checkpoint, and the new four-page SGA 1 English checkpoint.\n\nSGA 1 addition: file 00a is a bounded source-audited English working checkpoint for the Expose I heading/opening and section I.1. Its sole authority is the corrected French TeX in arXiv math/0206203v2, exact main-file lines 556-604. Continuation begins at line 605, section I.2, Morphismes quasi-finis. File 07 groups all 20 public-safe files: editable TeX, five source/control ledgers, compact build records, four target-page renders, continuation cursor, attribution and scope notes, manifests, and exact hashes.\n\nSGA 1 boundary: this is one machine-assisted source-audited working unit. It is not complete SGA 1, a critical edition, peer review, mathematical certification, or independent scholarly certification. External English candidates were wording/adverse controls only and are neither source authority nor independently corroborating witnesses.\n\nSGA 5 boundary: the public English reader is substantial source-aware working material, but its readiness audit remains open. Known editorial and source-ambiguity items remain documented; the file is not a critical edition or independent certification of every locus. Historical Spanish SGA 5 checkpoints remain withdrawn pending a canonical rebuild and are absent from this version.\n\nSGA 6 boundary: the corrected English reader covers the extant scan with explicit authority layers. The prefix is inherited and partially synchronized; idx532-662 was synchronized against the directly checked French layer available at build time; idx663-702 and terminal matter are scan-checked draft material pending later French reconciliation. The French reader is a source-rescribe checkpoint at idx684, not whole-volume certification. The Spanish file is a bounded four-page tranche.\n\nUse: open the reader PDFs first. Use the ZIP files for editable TeX, source/reference material, ledgers, build and render evidence, and checksums. Build success establishes artifact integrity, not mathematical correctness. Verify citation-critical formulas, diagrams, tables, and theorem statements against the included source controls.\n\nCorrections and continuation: the inspectable GitHub mirror and correction channel are at https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts. None of these surfaces is called a critical edition, complete translation, proof check, diagram-by-diagram certification, or whole-SGA completion.",
    "version": "2026-07-18 SGA 6 support-archive privacy withdrawal; SGA 1/5/6 readers retained",
